==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sh|sla-pro|*grana}} (cognate with dialectal or obsolete Bulgarian {{m|bg|sc=Cyrl|гран}}/{{m|bg|sc=Cyrl|гранка}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|sh}}, cognate with German {{m|de|Granne||awn}}, Old English {{m|ang|granu||moustache}} and Old Norse {{m|non|grǫn||a pine tree}} ( > Danish {{m|da|gran||spruce}}). Compare Old Norse {{m|non|grein||branch}} ( > Danish {{m|da|gren}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡrǎːna/|lang=sh}}
* {{hyphenation|gra|na|lang=sh}}
* {{rhymes|ǎːna|lang=sh}}

